1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:45,837
IN MEMORY OF DIRECTOR AHN PANSUK

5
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:48,966
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

6
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:50,676
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

7
00:01:24,668 --> 00:01:27,796
[staff] Mr. Park Minjae, we're done.
Thank you for your patience.

8
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,132
Take your time getting up.

9
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:34,261
Take it slow, and hold onto this here.

10
00:01:41,143 --> 00:01:42,519
Let's try walking a few steps.

11
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:43,603
[Minjae] Yes.

12
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:46,481
[staff] You said it was a little tight,
so I made some adjustments.

13
00:01:46,565 --> 00:01:48,191
Go ahead and take a few steps.

14
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,236
Slowly. Yeah.

15
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:56,575
[staff] How is it? Is it okay?

16
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,827
Yeah. I think it's okay.

17
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:01,079
[doctor] It's clean.

18
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:06,335
Uh, does that mean I'm still in remission?

19
00:02:06,418 --> 00:02:07,919
[doctor] Yes, that's right.

20
00:02:08,003 --> 00:02:11,465
There's no sign of it spreading
anywhere else, and everything looks good.

21
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:12,716
Well, you're young, so...

22
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:18,055
After five years of complete remission,
you're generally considered cured.

23
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,598
You're 10 years in remission.

24
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:22,017
Keep up your regular check-ups,
and you'll be fine.

25
00:02:22,601 --> 00:02:24,561
But it's still cancer.

26
00:02:24,645 --> 00:02:27,606
Can I really
just let my guard down like that?

27
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:29,858
[doctor] Yes, eat well and exercise.

28
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,735
Just keep taking good care of yourself.

29
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:34,488
You can live just like anyone else.

30
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:37,282
Okay, I will.

31
00:02:38,075 --> 00:02:39,076
EPISODE 1

32
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:43,955
DON'T BRUSH YOUR TEETH
IN THE KITCHEN

33
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:46,333
Answer the phone. I'm brushing my teeth.

34
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,439
Hello.

35
00:03:10,107 --> 00:03:11,525
-Hel...
-[line beeping]

36
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:13,819
Damn it.

37
00:03:16,405 --> 00:03:18,240
You could've picked that up.

38
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:20,909
-They'll call back if it's urgent.
-[keyboard clacking]

39
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:23,203
-[Hangyeol] I was brushing my teeth.
-[phone vibrates]

40
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:28,875
That was Minjae just now.

41
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:30,794
Huh? Why?

42
00:03:31,545 --> 00:03:32,921
[Hangyeol] "Why aren't you picking up?

43
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:35,132
Do you all want to go to Dieland together?

44
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:37,759
How is the finite element analysis
coming along?"

45
00:03:38,552 --> 00:03:39,678
That's his text.

46
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:42,305
We haven't even touched it.

47
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:45,684
What should we say?

48
00:03:48,019 --> 00:03:52,315
Should I say we're not done yet,
but we're almost there?

49
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:53,650
No, wait.

50
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,360
Let me... [sighs]

51
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:56,611
Let me text him.

52
00:03:58,363 --> 00:03:59,364
EOM TAEHO

53
00:04:00,991 --> 00:04:02,242
[Taeho] <i>Watch your language.</i>

54
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:04,411
[announcer on PA] <i>A train is approaching.</i>

55
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:08,498
<i>Please take a step back</i>
<i>from the platform edge.</i>

56
00:04:10,459 --> 00:04:11,460
Jeez.

57
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:47,370
GORI'S SHOES

58
00:06:49,034 --> 00:06:50,243
She's going to fall.

59
00:06:50,327 --> 00:06:51,328
-[grunts]
-[thuds]

60
00:07:27,989 --> 00:07:28,990
[Minjae] Excuse me.

61
00:07:29,658 --> 00:07:30,659
Drink this...

62
00:07:33,328 --> 00:07:34,621
and use this to wipe it off.

63
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:36,915
I'm okay.

64
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:39,542
No, at least get
the dirt and sand off for now.

65
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:43,713
If not cleaned right away,
it could lead to ulcers and infection.

66
00:07:44,214 --> 00:07:45,215
Wipe it off.

67
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:49,761
It broke, right? Give it to me.

68
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:54,641
Oh?

69
00:07:57,686 --> 00:08:00,605
-[grunts]
-What... That one wasn't broken.

70
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:04,943
You see, bipedal walking...

71
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:08,488
Walking on two legs means lifting
two equal-length legs off the ground

72
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:12,325
one at a time, stepping with each,
and moving your body forward.

73
00:08:12,409 --> 00:08:14,744
But first, those two legs need
to be the same length

74
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,746
for you to stay balanced. See?

75
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:21,084
Like this, and like this.
That's how you walk. Got it?

76
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:22,168
Now try these on.

77
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,097
Try walking around in them.

78
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:44,357
There will always be another bus.

79
00:08:45,734 --> 00:08:47,235
Don't run. You could fall.

80
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:51,197
Well, it's...

81
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:19,434
[passenger] Hi.

82
00:09:53,051 --> 00:09:56,471
[announcer] <i>This stop</i>
<i>is the Engineering Building.</i>

83
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:59,390
<i>The next stop is the library main gate.</i>

84
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:43,476
I'm Kim Haeun.

85
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:44,561
[softly] Kim Haeun.

86
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:59,033
I'm Lee Seongha.

87
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:13,506
Your name?

88
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:15,758
Lim Youjin.

89
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:23,224
Ten pieces?

90
00:11:23,975 --> 00:11:24,976
[Youjin] Yes.

91
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,979
It's supposed to be
at least five patterns,

92
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,147
so I just kept going...

93
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:31,566
No wonder you're top of your class.

94
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:37,071
Go see Professor Kang Miran after class.
She asked you to stop by.

95
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:39,824
[Youjin] Okay.

96
00:11:46,873 --> 00:11:48,166
Do you know what's going on?

97
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:49,250
[Subin] What?

98
00:11:49,876 --> 00:11:52,086
Why does the professor want to see her?

99
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:57,508
Ah. It's probably about grad school.
She wants her to join her lab.

100
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:00,595
-Is that so?
-Yes.

101
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:03,598
How come I didn't know about it?

102
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:06,017
Uh...

103
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:10,521
You could've talked to me about this.

104
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:15,318
Nothing's been decided yet, so...

105
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:20,448
[Subin groans] Oh, no. That must hurt.

106
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:22,242
Yeah. Hey, thanks.

107
00:12:22,325 --> 00:12:23,326
[Subin] Sure.

108
00:12:26,037 --> 00:12:27,956
Put that on, and here's the pantyhose.

109
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,416
[Youjin in English] Thank you.

110
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:35,046
-[Subin in Korean] Should I do it for you?
-Hmm-mmm.

111
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:45,598
[Youjin] There.

112
00:12:47,809 --> 00:12:49,686
[Subin] How did you end up
hurting it this badly?

113
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:52,605
-By the way, is he handsome?
-Hmm?

114
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:58,027
Ah... Well, he's not
super handsome or anything.

115
00:12:58,528 --> 00:13:00,697
I'd say he's pretty average-looking,
but not bad.

116
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:02,031
[Subin] Mmm...

117
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:03,116
How tall is he?

118
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:04,826
He's pretty tall.

119
00:13:05,410 --> 00:13:07,996
Uh... He's pretty fit,
but on the skinny side.

120
00:13:08,079 --> 00:13:09,497
Ooh...

121
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:13,042
-He got off at the Engineering Building.
-[Subin gasps] Really?

122
00:13:13,126 --> 00:13:15,044
How come I've never seen him?

123
00:13:17,171 --> 00:13:19,007
Was it love at first sight? Like fate?

124
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:22,677
No. I'm just feeling grateful. That's all.

125
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:24,721
Hmm.

126
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:29,600
Well, if you run into him again,
that's got to be fate then.

127
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:33,187
We go to the same school.

128
00:13:33,271 --> 00:13:35,481
If we meet again,
it's coincidence, not fate.

129
00:13:38,109 --> 00:13:40,361
And I'm graduating soon anyway.

130
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:45,533
Youjin, are you sure
you don't want to go to grad school?

131
00:13:46,993 --> 00:13:48,661
Come on, let's go together.

132
00:13:48,745 --> 00:13:52,623
I want to study with you. Please?

133
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:54,292
Come on, join me.

134
00:13:54,375 --> 00:13:58,463
[groans] Youjin, let's study together.

135
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:04,218
-Come in.
-[door opens]

136
00:14:12,477 --> 00:14:14,312
It's you, Youjin. Come on in.

137
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:20,651
Have a seat.

138
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:31,662
Did you have the talk?
What did your parents say?

139
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:34,957
Ah, they said they were okay
with me going to grad school.

140
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:37,418
See? I told you.

141
00:14:37,502 --> 00:14:40,213
No parent would say no
to their kid wanting to study.

142
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:44,008
But I thought
maybe I should just get a job.

143
00:14:44,092 --> 00:14:45,343
There's the tuition...

144
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:47,762
Tuition? You've been
at the top of your class

145
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:50,473
and on scholarship this whole time.

146
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:52,558
What's there to worry about? Huh?

147
00:14:52,642 --> 00:14:55,269
Grad schools also offer tuition aid
for top students.

148
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:56,729
You don't have to worry.

149
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,610
I'm recommending this for a reason.

150
00:15:03,069 --> 00:15:06,364
I really think you're a better fit
for academia than the corporate world.

151
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:12,036
I'm not sure yet.

152
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:18,126
My grades are good,
but I haven't won any design competitions.

153
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:21,045
No matter how hard I try,
it doesn't work out.

154
00:15:21,129 --> 00:15:24,841
Honestly, sometimes I wonder if maybe
I just don't have a talent for this.

155
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:27,635
I don't know.

156
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:30,888
You just had bad luck with competitions.

157
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:35,560
And you can develop a talent for design
or creativity later in life, too.

158
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:37,103
That's what happened to me.

159
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:43,317
When I see you like this,
even your personality...

160
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:47,029
You really remind me of myself
when I was younger.

161
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:52,118
I had the exact same worries
back in undergrad.

162
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:55,288
Everyone around me was doing so well,

163
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:57,790
winning competitions
left and right, doing great.

164
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:02,211
I kept asking myself, "Why can't I
do it too, no matter how hard I try?"

165
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:06,966
But that's not how talent works.

166
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:09,051
Especially in academia,

167
00:16:09,135 --> 00:16:12,054
the more work you put in,
the more you get out of it.

168
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:14,473
And you know what?

169
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:18,978
Those people I used to envy?
Those talented kids?

170
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:22,231
Do you know how many of them
are still around now?

171
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:24,609
I'm the only one left.

172
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:31,908
The harder you work, Youjin,
the more you'll get out of it.

173
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:32,992
Trust me.

174
00:16:37,788 --> 00:16:39,373
I need a successor, too.

175
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:42,627
Someone who can take over after me.

176
00:16:43,169 --> 00:16:45,713
Someone I can trust
to pass everything on to.

177
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:51,219
I'll be able to guide you better.

178
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,139
-[Miran] Come in.
-[door opens]

179
00:16:55,223 --> 00:16:57,141
-Professor, it's Youngsoo.
-[Miran] Hey.

180
00:16:57,225 --> 00:17:00,353
Well, Reporter Lee is here.

181
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:02,188
-Okay.
-[door opens]

182
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:06,275
I have an interview and a photo shoot
with this magazine called <i>Lady Sense</i>.

183
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:07,777
-[Youjin] Ah.
-If you don't mind,

184
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,278
could you help me with it?

185
00:17:10,321 --> 00:17:11,447
Yes, I can help.

186
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:12,740
Good, thanks.

187
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:16,827
What's with your shoes, by the way?

188
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:18,537
[Youjin] Ah...

189
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:28,839
[Youngsoo] Hey,
are you shopping or what? Hurry up.

190
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,385
-[Youjin] Okay.
-[Youngsoo] And bring this too, okay?

191
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:33,469
[Youjin] Okay.

192
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:41,561
This time, the concept
is "A Thousand Wishes."

193
00:17:42,478 --> 00:17:45,565
So, just like folding
a thousand paper cranes,

194
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:48,651
we're knitting a thousand hats
to donate to children in war zones,

195
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:51,404
each one carrying a wish for peace.

196
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:56,158
When you fold paper cranes, each crane...

197
00:17:56,242 --> 00:17:59,036
Aren't these the hats we made
for our assignment?

198
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:00,329
Were they for donation?

199
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:04,292
Why didn't she tell us?

200
00:18:04,959 --> 00:18:06,752
Is the donation under the school's name?

201
00:18:06,836 --> 00:18:10,423
Come on. The professor's name
is basically the school's name.

202
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:18,180
The triangle, you know.

203
00:18:19,056 --> 00:18:23,060
That place in Africa where Cleopatra...

204
00:18:23,144 --> 00:18:24,145
[reporter] You mean Egypt?

205
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:25,646
Not Egypt.

206
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:26,731
[reporter] What?

207
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:29,483
Not Egypt.

208
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:33,362
Ah! I meant a pyramid.

209
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:35,698
[reporter] Ah... Pyramid.

210
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:38,659
You know the symmetrical triangle, right?

211
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:44,332
Just have me sit right
at the very top of it.

212
00:18:44,915 --> 00:18:45,916
What?

213
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:55,801
Professor,
could you move over just a little?

214
00:18:56,385 --> 00:19:00,890
When this gets bound,
the photo might get folded.

215
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:06,479
We agreed to run one shot
across two full pages.

216
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:07,688
We already talked about this.

217
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:11,150
Right. We will have one shot
across two pages, but--

218
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:12,276
[Miran] Exactly.

219
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:14,904
We don't need a bunch of little shots.

220
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:18,032
Let's do one big shot.
Warm, but charismatic.

221
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:20,701
I want the concept
to come through in one photo.

222
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:24,288
Yes, I'm all for doing one shot.
I just wanted to say...

223
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:28,709
I think it'd be better if you could
move just a little to the side.

224
00:19:29,794 --> 00:19:33,839
Then the pyramid won't have
as much charisma.

225
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,467
Ah, but...

226
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:37,718
Hmm...

227
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:42,640
Once this gets bound,

228
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:46,227
there could be a problem
with the part that folds.

229
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:48,646
So, if you could move
just a little to the side--

230
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,606
Then it won't be a pyramid anymore.

231
00:19:51,941 --> 00:19:53,776
[yells] Warm charisma!

232
00:19:59,115 --> 00:20:01,033
How many times do I have to repeat myself?

233
00:20:02,159 --> 00:20:04,829
[reporter] All right, then...

234
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:06,455
Let's start the shoot.

235
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:08,916
[softly] Just do it.

236
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:13,713
[photographer] All right, very good.
Look here. Okay.

237
00:20:13,796 --> 00:20:15,881
-One, two.
-[camera shutter clicks]

238
00:20:15,965 --> 00:20:19,218
Now, give me a smile.
Yes, very good. Okay, one, two.

239
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,930
All right. Warm charisma.

240
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:25,099
Yes, very good. Okay. One, two.

241
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:29,770
[whispering] By the way,
we don't have a thousand, do we?

242
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:33,190
I don't think
there are a thousand of them.

243
00:20:34,108 --> 00:20:36,402
That's 200 at most.

244
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:39,572
[whispers] 200 sounds about right.

245
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,200
[Taeho] It's 73.5 years.

246
00:20:43,284 --> 00:20:47,663
What do you think
the average human life expectancy will be

247
00:20:47,747 --> 00:20:50,332
by the time we reach that age?

248
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:51,876
-Well, something like...
-[Taeho] Yeah?

249
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,335
...90, I think?

250
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:55,379
-[Taeho] What do you think, Chansoo?
-100?

251
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:58,382
No, it's 120 years.

252
00:20:58,883 --> 00:20:59,884
[Chansoo] Ah.

253
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:02,303
At the current rate
of medical advancement,

254
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:04,764
human life expectancy
will increase that much.

255
00:21:04,847 --> 00:21:05,848
[Minjae] Oh, man.

256
00:21:05,931 --> 00:21:08,392
Isn't that a good thing?
It's good to live longer.

257
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,020
Well... [clears throat]

258
00:21:11,562 --> 00:21:13,355
it's not just about living longer anymore.

259
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:16,817
From now on,
it'll be about how you live your life.

260
00:21:16,901 --> 00:21:20,362
[Chansoo] He's right.
Living too long can be boring.

261
00:21:21,238 --> 00:21:22,573
This year was so boring.

262
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:24,867
-It wasn't fun at all.
-[Taeho] Right.

263
00:21:25,743 --> 00:21:27,244
You guys are all talk.

264
00:21:27,328 --> 00:21:29,997
Come on, stop talking
and actually do something.

265
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:33,584
Hey, that's what we've been talking about.

266
00:21:34,335 --> 00:21:38,923
Exactly. Stop the jibber-jabber
and actually do something.

267
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:44,261
I mean, did you even get a single
decent result from this beta test?

268
00:21:44,345 --> 00:21:45,387
I think I'm finished.

269
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:50,476
I don't have any report
to upload to the archive.

270
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:54,730
How do we not have a single paper
with an impact factor of 7?

271
00:21:54,814 --> 00:21:57,483
We're dead last
in the entire school right now!

272
00:21:57,566 --> 00:21:58,567
Minjae.

273
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:03,239
We were talking about life.

274
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:05,115
Yeah, exactly. Life...

275
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:07,660
Guys, this is about life.

276
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:12,206
I don't know how much longer I'll be able
to keep working with you here in the lab.

277
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:16,335
I don't know how long my body
and my health will allow me to keep going.

278
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:19,171
So...

279
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:26,095
we really have to finish Danny
before I die. Okay?

280
00:22:28,848 --> 00:22:30,307
You're gaslighting us again.

281
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,059
What did you just say?

282
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:35,271
[sighs] It's been 10 years
since you were cured.

283
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:36,730
You're healthier than I am.

284
00:22:38,524 --> 00:22:39,942
-Hey.
-[Taeho] Now, I'm sicker than you.

285
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:42,862
-How many times do I say it?
-[Taeho] I bet you'll live longer than me.

286
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:46,866
With cancer, there's no such thing
as a complete cure.

287
00:22:46,949 --> 00:22:48,659
[Taeho] No, you're completely cured.

288
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:51,036
What... No.

289
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:52,621
So, Minjae...

290
00:22:53,873 --> 00:22:56,166
what I'm trying to say is,

291
00:22:56,250 --> 00:23:01,130
we have lives
outside of school, too. Okay?

292
00:23:02,548 --> 00:23:05,301
Just like you write an experimental plan
for the new year,

293
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:07,511
we could write one for our lives.

294
00:23:07,595 --> 00:23:08,679
That's what I'm talking about.

295
00:23:08,762 --> 00:23:10,931
[Hangyeol] I think it's a great idea.

296
00:23:11,015 --> 00:23:15,311
How about we make a list of things
we want to do, like a bucket list?

297
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:21,483
It could be traveling the world,
or just simply traveling.

298
00:23:22,860 --> 00:23:26,113
Or Michelin food.
Going to a Michelin restaurant.

299
00:23:27,156 --> 00:23:32,494
Or a girlfriend.
Yeah, getting a girlfriend.

300
00:23:32,578 --> 00:23:35,414
I'd like that. Dating. Getting married.

301
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:38,751
[chuckling] Yeah, exactly.
Something like that.

302
00:23:38,834 --> 00:23:39,835
Yeah? Minjae.

303
00:23:39,919 --> 00:23:41,545
[Minjae] I don't need anything else.

304
00:23:42,129 --> 00:23:45,215
Before I die, I just want our Danny to...

305
00:23:45,299 --> 00:23:46,800
-[Taeho sighs]
-[Hangyeol sighs]

306
00:23:46,884 --> 00:23:50,387
-I'm just...
-[Taeho sighing]

307
00:23:50,471 --> 00:23:52,806
I mean... Guys, seriously?

308
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:33,305
PARK MINJAE'S BUCKET LIST
1. EAT CHICKEN

309
00:24:33,389 --> 00:24:35,808
1. EAT CHICKEN - DONE

310
00:24:41,397 --> 00:24:43,357
2. 100 PISTOL SQUATS - DONE

311
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:47,444
3. GET A DRIVER'S LICENSE
4. BUY A CAR

312
00:24:47,528 --> 00:24:51,323
5. TRAVEL THE WORLD
6. START DATING

313
00:24:54,159 --> 00:24:57,371
6. START DATING... ASK SOMEONE OUT?

314
00:25:12,886 --> 00:25:17,349
FRIENDS

315
00:25:17,433 --> 00:25:18,434
CHACHA

316
00:25:24,189 --> 00:25:26,400
[Minjae] <i>Chacha, what are you up to?</i>

317
00:25:45,169 --> 00:25:46,170
Hello?

318
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:49,506
Hey, I was about to leave work.

319
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:54,428
It's pretty busy because it's the end
of the year. What's up?

320
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:57,097
It's just been a while
since we last saw each other.

321
00:25:57,890 --> 00:25:59,808
I thought we could grab a bite to eat.

322
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:03,520
But you seem busy.

323
00:26:04,104 --> 00:26:06,273
Let's meet up when things slow down a bit.

324
00:26:11,737 --> 00:26:12,738
Really?

325
00:26:14,656 --> 00:26:15,657
Are you sure?

326
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:16,742
Let's meet up.

327
00:26:18,786 --> 00:26:21,330
Yeah. In front of the school.

328
00:26:22,456 --> 00:26:25,167
I know that place. When?

329
00:26:29,171 --> 00:26:31,215
Okay. I'll see you then.

330
00:26:32,466 --> 00:26:33,842
Okay. Bye.

331
00:27:31,191 --> 00:27:33,193
FLOWERS

332
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:41,159
-[staff] Hello.
-Hello.

333
00:27:41,243 --> 00:27:42,244
-Hi.
-I...

334
00:27:42,870 --> 00:27:45,122
I want to buy some flowers.

335
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:46,748
[staff] Anything specific in mind?

336
00:27:47,249 --> 00:27:48,375
Uh...

337
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:50,878
I've never bought flowers before, so...

338
00:27:50,961 --> 00:27:53,213
[staff] Is it for your girlfriend?

339
00:27:53,297 --> 00:27:56,008
-What?
-[staff] Or for a birthday or a proposal?

340
00:27:56,091 --> 00:27:57,926
Oh, no. Not girlfriend.

341
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,304
Just a friend.

342
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:01,722
In that case...

343
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:06,476
We've got hydrangeas, lilies,
or carnations. They're gorgeous.

344
00:28:08,270 --> 00:28:09,980
Can I just get the roses over there?

345
00:28:10,063 --> 00:28:12,316
Sure. Which color would you like?

346
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:14,818
We've got red, yellow, and white.

347
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,321
Red, please.

348
00:28:17,404 --> 00:28:18,989
Got it.

349
00:28:28,332 --> 00:28:29,791
Hello.

350
00:28:29,875 --> 00:28:31,001
[staff] Hello.

351
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:33,253
I'm from the Department
of Fashion and Textiles.

352
00:28:33,337 --> 00:28:34,338
[staff] One moment, please.

353
00:28:34,421 --> 00:28:36,173
-Here you are.
-Thank you.

354
00:28:42,512 --> 00:28:44,097
[Subin] Youjin.
The flower basket is ready.

355
00:28:44,181 --> 00:28:45,182
Okay.

356
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:48,185
-Hey, one moment.
-What?

357
00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:49,269
What is it?

358
00:29:00,364 --> 00:29:01,406
Hmm...

359
00:29:03,951 --> 00:29:05,535
What's up? Someone you know?

360
00:29:06,036 --> 00:29:07,037
Hmm.

361
00:29:13,210 --> 00:29:15,879
Hi, Youngsoo. I'm at the flower shop now.

362
00:29:17,214 --> 00:29:18,215
What?

363
00:29:20,926 --> 00:29:22,052
Okay, <i>oppa.</i>

364
00:29:22,135 --> 00:29:25,138
All right. Bye.

365
00:29:28,266 --> 00:29:29,267
Kim Youngsoo?

366
00:29:29,351 --> 00:29:30,352
Yes.

367
00:29:30,894 --> 00:29:32,229
Why do you call him <i>oppa?</i>

368
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:34,690
I don't know. He told me to.

369
00:29:35,816 --> 00:29:38,151
We're close,
so I guess I can call him that.

370
00:29:38,986 --> 00:29:40,320
You're not close at all.

371
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:42,531
Not with you.

372
00:29:43,532 --> 00:29:46,201
That obnoxious bastard.
If only he wasn't my senior...

373
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,662
He's a good person, though.

374
00:29:49,663 --> 00:29:51,832
What? He's a good person?

375
00:29:51,915 --> 00:29:53,333
[customer] Thank you. Bye.

376
00:29:53,417 --> 00:29:54,918
-[staff] Have a good one.
-[customer] Thanks.

377
00:30:04,219 --> 00:30:05,721
-[Youngsoo] Hello.
-Hello.

378
00:30:06,596 --> 00:30:08,140
Do you want them in a bag?

379
00:30:08,223 --> 00:30:10,392
No, I'll put them here.

380
00:30:33,707 --> 00:30:34,708
Hey.

381
00:30:36,543 --> 00:30:37,544
Yeah.

382
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:41,089
How long?

383
00:30:41,882 --> 00:30:43,050
No, take your time.

384
00:30:44,801 --> 00:30:47,054
Yeah, I know that place.
Should I go there?

385
00:30:49,806 --> 00:30:50,807
Uh...

386
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:54,936
Of course. That works too.

387
00:30:55,645 --> 00:30:58,482
Then I'll head over there.
I'll see you there.

388
00:30:59,566 --> 00:31:00,567
Okay.

389
00:31:43,944 --> 00:31:46,113
-[Seohyun] Hello, ma'am.
-Hello.

390
00:31:48,365 --> 00:31:50,784
-I'm here for an inspection today.
-[owner] Okay.

391
00:31:50,867 --> 00:31:53,370
[Seohyun] First, just check
that the lens is clean.

392
00:31:53,453 --> 00:31:56,540
Then make sure
it's being charged every day.

393
00:31:56,623 --> 00:31:57,707
Okay.

394
00:31:57,791 --> 00:32:00,836
And this is checking
if it's moving properly,

395
00:32:00,919 --> 00:32:03,797
and if it's moving smoothly
in a straight line.

396
00:32:03,880 --> 00:32:07,968
And when you clean it,
be careful about the wheels.

397
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:10,262
-[owner] Okay, got it.
-Could you sign here?

398
00:32:12,556 --> 00:32:13,807
-Thank you.
-Sure.

399
00:32:13,890 --> 00:32:14,933
All right.

400
00:32:15,517 --> 00:32:16,643
Hey.

401
00:32:16,726 --> 00:32:18,562
-[Seohyun] I'm sorry I'm late.
-No, don't worry.

402
00:32:19,563 --> 00:32:21,648
This is Nam Yoonsoo,
my marketing team leader.

403
00:32:21,731 --> 00:32:24,234
This is Park Minjae,
my best friend from school.

404
00:32:24,317 --> 00:32:25,777
Hello, I've heard a lot about you.

405
00:32:25,861 --> 00:32:26,862
Hello, okay.

406
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:30,782
We're swamped with product launches
for the spring moving season.

407
00:32:30,866 --> 00:32:31,867
[Yoonsoo] Yeah.

408
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:33,201
Right. What do you think?

409
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:35,036
[Minjae] Hmm.

410
00:32:35,829 --> 00:32:36,913
It's nice.

411
00:32:37,747 --> 00:32:40,000
We're testing it out right now
before the launch.

412
00:32:40,083 --> 00:32:42,210
The display is 1080 by 1920.

413
00:32:44,838 --> 00:32:46,506
How much does it weigh? It looks heavy.

414
00:32:46,590 --> 00:32:48,258
Yeah, 65.

415
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:50,927
-[Minjae] Oh...
-It's quite heavy because of the display.

416
00:32:51,469 --> 00:32:55,390
It takes five hours to charge
and can run for 12 to 15 hours.

417
00:32:57,184 --> 00:32:59,895
So you and Ms. Cha went
to the same high school?

418
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:02,355
-[Minjae] Yes.
-And the same college too?

419
00:33:02,981 --> 00:33:05,525
Right, yeah. It's a funny coincidence.

420
00:33:06,109 --> 00:33:08,987
But I took the college
entrance exam four times,

421
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:11,031
so I barely ever ran into her...

422
00:33:11,865 --> 00:33:14,117
I started school years ahead of him.

423
00:33:14,201 --> 00:33:17,287
He should be treating me like a senior,

424
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:20,165
but I get no respect because we went
to high school together.

425
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:22,209
Come on, I treated you like a senior.

426
00:33:23,752 --> 00:33:24,794
When?

427
00:33:25,795 --> 00:33:28,757
Should I tell him how you got drunk
and threw up all the time,

428
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:30,467
and I always had to clean it up?

429
00:33:30,967 --> 00:33:32,594
She did that?

430
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:35,013
[Seohyun] Excuse me,
could we get the menu, please?

431
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:36,097
[owner] Okay.

432
00:33:39,392 --> 00:33:41,228
-No.
-[both chuckle]

433
00:33:41,811 --> 00:33:46,566
Now, let's hear a few words
from Professor Kang Miran,

434
00:33:46,650 --> 00:33:48,276
who's guided us all this time.

435
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:50,737
THANK YOU, PROFESSOR!
TEACHER APPRECIATION DINNER

436
00:33:52,822 --> 00:33:55,116
Hello, everyone. I'm Kang Miran.

437
00:33:56,493 --> 00:34:01,248
Department of Fashion and Textiles
has made it through another year.

438
00:34:01,831 --> 00:34:05,043
Thanks to the faculty,
my seniors and juniors,

439
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:08,546
we are sending off
another outstanding group of graduates.

440
00:34:09,923 --> 00:34:11,841
To all of you
leaving the university behind

441
00:34:11,925 --> 00:34:13,760
to make your way in the world,

442
00:34:14,511 --> 00:34:17,347
now is the time to go out there

443
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:20,558
and pursue your ideals freely
and to the fullest.

444
00:34:21,309 --> 00:34:24,312
You can do it. Go out there
and achieve your goals.

445
00:34:25,939 --> 00:34:28,400
Of course, the world can be a harsh place.

446
00:34:29,025 --> 00:34:33,905
There will be times
when you stumble or experience failure.

447
00:34:34,698 --> 00:34:36,283
But don't be afraid.

448
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:40,954
You have me and the university behind you.

449
00:34:41,538 --> 00:34:44,874
Even after you leave,
all of us who came before you

450
00:34:44,958 --> 00:34:49,004
and those who will come after you
remain closely and firmly connected.

451
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:53,425
So don't be afraid,
take your perseverance and pride,

452
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:55,260
and confidently go out into the world.

453
00:34:56,720 --> 00:35:00,098
But don't become arrogant.

454
00:35:00,682 --> 00:35:02,350
The more accomplished you become,

455
00:35:02,434 --> 00:35:05,520
the more important it is
to remain humble and compassionate.

456
00:35:06,521 --> 00:35:09,774
If you stay humble
and keep working diligently,

457
00:35:09,858 --> 00:35:13,111
you will definitely achieve your dreams.

458
00:35:15,822 --> 00:35:18,533
-That turned into a bit of a lecture.
-No, not at all.

459
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:22,454
But this is the last time you'll have
to listen to one after you graduate,

460
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:23,538
so bear with me.

461
00:35:29,002 --> 00:35:32,505
Ah, and I have
some more good news to share.

462
00:35:32,589 --> 00:35:35,091
Our very own Kim Youngsoo

463
00:35:35,175 --> 00:35:37,886
will be joining Nagoya University
as an assistant professor.

464
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:41,514
It's all thanks to you, Professor.
Thank you.

465
00:35:41,598 --> 00:35:42,599
Thank you.

466
00:35:45,226 --> 00:35:47,729
-Remember that promise we made?
-[Minjae] What?

467
00:35:47,812 --> 00:35:50,857
If neither of us were married after 40,
we'd save each other.

468
00:35:51,441 --> 00:35:52,442
-Stop.
-[Seohyun laughs]

469
00:35:52,525 --> 00:35:54,319
You made a promise like that?

470
00:35:56,071 --> 00:35:59,658
But, Minjae, I don't think
you could get married even after 40.

471
00:35:59,741 --> 00:36:01,534
Seriously, what are you going to do?

472
00:36:01,618 --> 00:36:02,869
Are you single now?

473
00:36:02,952 --> 00:36:03,953
Ah.

474
00:36:05,372 --> 00:36:06,373
[exhales] Yes.

475
00:36:06,456 --> 00:36:09,125
But why? You're attractive

476
00:36:09,209 --> 00:36:10,794
and have a PhD from Seohan National.

477
00:36:10,877 --> 00:36:12,754
I'm sure you're popular with women.

478
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:16,216
I don't have a PhD.
I haven't gotten my degree yet.

479
00:36:16,299 --> 00:36:18,760
Maybe you're too picky.

480
00:36:20,053 --> 00:36:23,640
I've tried setting him up with coworkers
and friends, but he always says no.

481
00:36:23,723 --> 00:36:26,768
His standards are way up here.
They're way too high.

482
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:28,436
Maybe he doesn't like blind dates.

483
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:30,355
Maybe he prefers
meeting people organically.

484
00:36:30,438 --> 00:36:32,857
Organic or not,
he has to actually meet people first.

485
00:36:32,941 --> 00:36:34,901
Minjae doesn't even try.

486
00:36:34,984 --> 00:36:38,446
If you're done eating, let's go.
I know you're busy.

487
00:36:39,489 --> 00:36:40,490
[Yoonsoo] I got this.

488
00:36:40,573 --> 00:36:41,658
No, I'll...

489
00:36:41,741 --> 00:36:43,451
No, I can pay.

490
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:45,995
Why?

491
00:36:47,497 --> 00:36:49,290
[Minjae] Come on, I want to pay.

492
00:36:50,333 --> 00:36:52,460
A student doesn't have any money.
Let him pay.

493
00:36:52,544 --> 00:36:54,295
-I have money.
-[Seohyun] What?

494
00:36:58,591 --> 00:36:59,926
Are you two dating?

495
00:37:00,009 --> 00:37:02,595
No, not really.
But there's something going on.

496
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:04,305
I see.

497
00:37:05,473 --> 00:37:08,435
He's kind, but he's kind of clueless.

498
00:37:10,228 --> 00:37:12,147
A nice guy is the best.

499
00:37:12,731 --> 00:37:14,357
He is really nice.

500
00:37:14,441 --> 00:37:15,775
Hmm.

501
00:37:16,359 --> 00:37:17,610
What do you think of him?

502
00:37:18,319 --> 00:37:20,613
They say guys know other guys best, right?

503
00:37:20,697 --> 00:37:22,949
If you think he's okay,
I'll give him a chance.

504
00:37:24,909 --> 00:37:29,205
So you'll go out with him if I say yes,
and you won't if I say no?

505
00:37:29,706 --> 00:37:30,707
Yes.

506
00:37:32,709 --> 00:37:33,752
If you like him,

507
00:37:35,128 --> 00:37:37,130
I like him.

508
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:40,508
If you want to go out with him, go for it.

509
00:37:41,342 --> 00:37:42,510
Really?

510
00:37:45,305 --> 00:37:46,306
Oh.

511
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:48,975
I'll go get the car. Wait here.

512
00:37:50,477 --> 00:37:51,936
Come out when I call you.

513
00:38:01,029 --> 00:38:02,197
[Seohyun] Thank you, bye.

514
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:04,532
-[owner] Bye. Come again.
-[Seohyun] I will.

515
00:38:05,325 --> 00:38:07,285
So you'll be an assistant professor there?

516
00:38:07,786 --> 00:38:09,412
When? From this semester?

517
00:38:10,163 --> 00:38:11,247
No.

518
00:38:12,081 --> 00:38:13,458
I'm starting next semester.

519
00:38:14,793 --> 00:38:16,961
But it all happened so suddenly,

520
00:38:17,045 --> 00:38:18,713
I haven't had time
to prepare for anything.

521
00:38:18,797 --> 00:38:20,215
I'm so overwhelmed right now.

522
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:21,758
You must be so busy.

523
00:38:23,426 --> 00:38:25,428
I'm happy for you, though.
Congratulations.

524
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:39,734
So... Nagoya University
is in Japan, right?

525
00:38:39,818 --> 00:38:41,027
Where in Japan is it?

526
00:38:42,570 --> 00:38:45,156
In Nagoya, obviously.
It's called Nagoya University.

527
00:38:45,782 --> 00:38:46,783
Are you dumb?

528
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:55,250
I mean, Jeju National University
is in Jeju Island.

529
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:57,669
Pusan National University is in Busan.

530
00:38:57,752 --> 00:39:01,005
Where's Daegu University?
In Daegu, obviously.

531
00:39:01,631 --> 00:39:04,592
Why do you say such dumb things?

532
00:39:09,222 --> 00:39:11,266
[Youjin] Not all of Jeju
is Jeju National University.

533
00:39:11,766 --> 00:39:14,143
There are different regions
in there, like Jeju City.

534
00:39:15,353 --> 00:39:17,814
Why are you grilling me about the address?

535
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:20,567
Who are you? Are you a district mayor?

536
00:39:21,109 --> 00:39:22,819
A community center employee?

537
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:24,445
Why pick a fight on a good day?

538
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:27,323
-I didn't pick a--
-[Subin] I need to use the restroom.

539
00:39:29,826 --> 00:39:32,120
-I should get going too.
-Hey.

540
00:39:35,874 --> 00:39:37,792
[Youngsoo] Professor, are you heading out?

541
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:47,176
Youngsoo, Subin,
thanks so much for preparing the event.

542
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:50,179
-[both chuckle]
-[Subin] Please. We didn't do anything.

543
00:39:51,055 --> 00:39:54,309
Right, Professor.
This... It's nothing much.

544
00:39:54,392 --> 00:39:56,895
Just a gift and some letters
from the students.

545
00:39:56,978 --> 00:39:58,938
[exclaims] Why did you even take those?

546
00:39:59,022 --> 00:40:01,399
[Youngsoo] No,
they're really just letters.

547
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:04,861
Ah, and these are some pastries.

548
00:40:05,653 --> 00:40:10,909
They're from Maman Bakery, your favorite.
You only eat their pastries.

549
00:40:11,492 --> 00:40:15,246
They're for when you get hungry
while working on your research later.

550
00:40:15,747 --> 00:40:17,582
Gosh, being this kind should be illegal.

551
00:40:17,665 --> 00:40:20,418
[Youngsoo chuckling] It's nothing.
It's cold out. You should head home.

552
00:40:20,501 --> 00:40:23,630
[Miran] Okay, sure. Thank you.

553
00:40:25,924 --> 00:40:27,258
[Youngsoo] I'll stay in touch, Professor.

554
00:40:27,342 --> 00:40:29,177
[Miran] Yeah, let's. Thank you.

555
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:31,596
-Thanks, Subin. Okay.
-I'll put it here. No worries.

556
00:40:32,764 --> 00:40:34,891
-Thank you.
-All right, get back home safe!

557
00:40:34,974 --> 00:40:36,351
Have a safe trip home. Bye.

558
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:38,353
Please get her home safely, sir.

559
00:40:44,776 --> 00:40:47,403
These little suck-ups.

560
00:40:48,696 --> 00:40:49,739
Hey, Subin.

561
00:40:49,822 --> 00:40:50,823
[Subin] Yes?

562
00:40:52,825 --> 00:40:54,118
How about we go grab one more drink?

563
00:40:54,702 --> 00:40:55,703
Ah...

564
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:59,791
I don't know.
You look pretty drunk already.

565
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:01,334
What do you mean, I'm drunk?

566
00:41:01,960 --> 00:41:06,673
Okay, then just beer...
let's go have just one more beer.

567
00:41:07,715 --> 00:41:09,801
I'll ask Youjin too, then.

568
00:41:09,884 --> 00:41:11,260
No.

569
00:41:12,804 --> 00:41:15,098
Let's just go without Youjin.
Just the two of us.

570
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:16,182
Oh...

571
00:41:40,081 --> 00:41:41,165
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

572
00:41:41,749 --> 00:41:43,042
Where's the restroom?

573
00:41:43,126 --> 00:41:44,877
It's over there, in the back.

574
00:41:44,961 --> 00:41:45,962
Thank you.

575
00:42:01,102 --> 00:42:02,979
I almost made a total fool of myself.

576
00:42:03,062 --> 00:42:04,897
I'd never live it down. [groans]

577
00:42:23,041 --> 00:42:24,042
Hi.

578
00:42:25,126 --> 00:42:26,335
What's your name?

579
00:42:29,714 --> 00:42:32,175
[robot] <i>Hello, my name is Arti.</i>

580
00:42:32,258 --> 00:42:34,052
<i>How can I help you?</i>

581
00:42:41,768 --> 00:42:43,061
-[staff] Excuse me.
-Yes?

582
00:42:43,144 --> 00:42:45,480
[staff] Just leave it. We can do it later.

583
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:47,065
No. I'm almost done.

584
00:43:08,086 --> 00:43:09,170
[Youjin] Hey, what's going on?

585
00:43:09,253 --> 00:43:10,296
Hey, wait!

586
00:43:16,511 --> 00:43:17,553
Jeez! What the hell?

587
00:43:17,637 --> 00:43:19,555
-Somebody call the police! Now!
-[Youngsoo grunting]

588
00:43:19,639 --> 00:43:21,349
-What? Police.
-[Youjin] Hurry!

589
00:43:21,432 --> 00:43:22,517
[Youngsoo] That hurts!

590
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,352
-Call the police... No, let me.
-[Youngsoo groans]

591
00:43:24,936 --> 00:43:27,230
-[Youjin] Hurry!
-[Youngsoo] That hurts. [groans]

592
00:43:30,149 --> 00:43:33,694
Whoa. It's right around the corner,
but we're not moving an inch.

593
00:43:33,778 --> 00:43:37,865
Was there perhaps an accident?
The alleys around here are very narrow.

594
00:43:38,866 --> 00:43:41,035
I should call and tell him
to cross the road.

595
00:43:51,712 --> 00:43:52,964
-Oh.
-[Youjin] It's okay.

596
00:43:53,047 --> 00:43:54,090
Hello?

597
00:43:54,674 --> 00:43:55,675
Ah.

598
00:43:56,467 --> 00:43:59,595
I'm okay. I left early.

599
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:03,015
Yeah. I didn't get to say goodbye.

600
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:05,184
Mmm.

601
00:44:06,144 --> 00:44:07,145
Mmm.

602
00:44:09,397 --> 00:44:10,398
Ah.

603
00:44:10,481 --> 00:44:14,277
You're driving now,
so let's talk later. Okay, bye.

604
00:44:19,448 --> 00:44:22,493
Hey, thank you for helping us.

605
00:44:23,744 --> 00:44:25,037
Don't worry about it.

606
00:44:25,121 --> 00:44:26,747
But are you really okay?

607
00:44:27,540 --> 00:44:29,125
Did you hurt yourself anywhere?

608
00:44:30,626 --> 00:44:32,253
No, I'm okay. I'm fine.

609
00:44:33,129 --> 00:44:35,173
GWANAK CENTRAL POLICE STATION

610
00:44:35,256 --> 00:44:37,842
So the three of you go to the same school?

611
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:40,428
Yes, but we're in different departments.

612
00:44:41,304 --> 00:44:43,556
I don't study Fashion.
I study something else.

613
00:44:44,557 --> 00:44:45,558
[officer] What do you study?

614
00:44:45,641 --> 00:44:47,226
-Mechanical engineering.
-[officer] Ah.

615
00:44:47,310 --> 00:44:49,187
-A graduate student. Okay.
-[officer] Okay.

616
00:44:50,271 --> 00:44:52,356
Do we have to hire a lawyer or something?

617
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:54,400
That's what they do in TV shows.

618
00:44:54,483 --> 00:44:59,197
We're interviewing you as a witness,
not a suspect, so you won't need a lawyer.

619
00:44:59,280 --> 00:45:01,866
Detective. Please make sure

620
00:45:01,949 --> 00:45:05,494
that bastard gets the maximum sentence
and never gets out.

621
00:45:06,412 --> 00:45:07,538
-[officer] Okay.
-[shudders]

622
00:45:07,622 --> 00:45:11,959
Then just tell me exactly what you saw.
You can take your time.

623
00:45:13,544 --> 00:45:15,504
So, when I went in...

624
00:45:15,588 --> 00:45:18,591
[exhales] ...that bastard
had Subin pinned against the wall

625
00:45:18,674 --> 00:45:20,593
and was trying to force a kiss on her.

626
00:45:21,302 --> 00:45:25,348
She was saying no,
but he just kept forcing himself on her.

627
00:45:25,431 --> 00:45:27,642
He shoved her
against the wall with his body,

628
00:45:27,725 --> 00:45:29,560
pinned her arms so she couldn't move,

629
00:45:30,519 --> 00:45:32,480
and then he forced a kiss on her.

630
00:45:32,563 --> 00:45:35,942
I mean, it wasn't a kiss.
It was sexual assault. Anyway...

631
00:45:36,943 --> 00:45:38,027
You saw it too, right?

632
00:45:38,486 --> 00:45:39,487
What?

633
00:45:40,780 --> 00:45:43,866
He's a witness. He was there with me.

634
00:45:44,367 --> 00:45:47,286
I'm telling the truth, right?
You saw it too, right?

635
00:45:50,790 --> 00:45:53,334
No, I didn't see it.

636
00:45:53,918 --> 00:45:55,419
You didn't see it?

637
00:45:55,503 --> 00:45:58,589
I mean, by the time I got there,
it was already over.

638
00:45:59,924 --> 00:46:02,927
Her friend got him
under control pretty quickly.

639
00:46:03,594 --> 00:46:07,390
She was on top of the guy,
who was lying on the ground.

640
00:46:10,559 --> 00:46:11,560
But...

641
00:46:12,603 --> 00:46:14,355
I did hear a scream.

642
00:46:14,939 --> 00:46:16,440
I think it was a woman screaming.

643
00:46:16,524 --> 00:46:19,694
Ah... All right. Got it.

644
00:46:23,322 --> 00:46:27,451
By the way, you were right there with us.
How could you not have seen it?

645
00:46:27,535 --> 00:46:32,039
Well, as I said, it was already over
when I got there.

646
00:46:32,123 --> 00:46:34,333
You got the situation
under control pretty quickly.

647
00:46:34,417 --> 00:46:35,710
But still...

648
00:46:35,793 --> 00:46:36,794
You could've said

649
00:46:37,420 --> 00:46:40,047
you thought I was telling the truth.

650
00:46:40,131 --> 00:46:42,383
Why did you say you didn't see anything?

651
00:46:42,466 --> 00:46:44,051
[Minjae] Because I didn't see it.

652
00:46:44,135 --> 00:46:45,970
I said I didn't see it because I didn't.

653
00:46:46,053 --> 00:46:47,555
I have to tell the truth.

654
00:46:48,055 --> 00:46:51,225
[Youjin] No, I'm not saying
you should've said you saw it.

655
00:46:52,059 --> 00:46:53,602
No, that's not what I meant.

656
00:46:56,772 --> 00:47:01,110
Besides, if I say the wrong thing,
I could be making a false accusation.

657
00:47:01,193 --> 00:47:03,988
Then there could be another victim.

658
00:47:04,071 --> 00:47:06,282
[Youjin] What do you mean, another victim?

659
00:47:06,866 --> 00:47:08,659
Are you siding with that asshole?

660
00:47:09,869 --> 00:47:11,370
I'm not siding with him.

661
00:47:11,454 --> 00:47:14,915
When you give a statement,
you have to get the facts straight.

662
00:47:17,460 --> 00:47:20,087
By the way, I saw you taking pictures.

663
00:47:21,464 --> 00:47:22,590
What?

664
00:47:22,673 --> 00:47:23,674
[Youjin] I saw it.

665
00:47:23,758 --> 00:47:25,926
You were taking pictures
in front of us earlier.

666
00:47:26,969 --> 00:47:29,930
-What about it?
-Can I see them?

667
00:47:30,014 --> 00:47:33,142
There might be something in there
we can use as evidence.

668
00:47:33,225 --> 00:47:34,643
There's nothing.

669
00:47:35,227 --> 00:47:37,980
I was just taking pictures
of the robot servers going around.

670
00:47:38,064 --> 00:47:40,983
I know. But you might've
caught something else in the shot.

671
00:47:41,067 --> 00:47:42,109
So please, let us see.

672
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:46,447
I'm not comfortable doing that.

673
00:47:47,615 --> 00:47:49,742
Why? What makes you uncomfortable?

674
00:47:49,825 --> 00:47:52,870
I mean, it's rude to ask to look
through someone's phone.

675
00:47:52,953 --> 00:47:55,915
No, I just want to see
if you happened to capture anything

676
00:47:55,998 --> 00:47:57,208
that could be evidence.

677
00:47:57,291 --> 00:47:58,334
I'm asking a favor.

678
00:47:58,417 --> 00:48:00,878
I said there's nothing.
You're making me uncomfortable.

679
00:48:00,961 --> 00:48:03,547
Right, why does that
make you uncomfortable?

680
00:48:03,631 --> 00:48:06,342
I just want to see the pictures.
You don't have weird photos, do you?

681
00:48:06,425 --> 00:48:08,719
What do you mean weird photos?
I don't have those.

682
00:48:08,803 --> 00:48:11,597
[Youjin] Yeah, exactly. So just show me.

683
00:48:13,349 --> 00:48:16,102
If you want to see it so badly,
go get a search warrant.

684
00:48:16,185 --> 00:48:17,228
Then I'll show you.

685
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:18,312
A search warrant...

686
00:48:21,232 --> 00:48:23,109
Come on, you're really being difficult.

687
00:48:24,193 --> 00:48:26,654
What? I'm the one being difficult here?

688
00:48:26,737 --> 00:48:30,408
I stepped in to help,
and now you're asking even more of me.

689
00:48:30,491 --> 00:48:33,035
What more am I asking?
I just want to see your phone.

690
00:48:33,994 --> 00:48:38,999
And when exactly did you help me?
I handled it all by myself.

691
00:48:39,583 --> 00:48:40,835
[weakly] Hey, Youjin.

692
00:48:40,918 --> 00:48:44,046
Hey. Are you okay? I'm sorry.

693
00:48:44,130 --> 00:48:46,006
Wait here. I'll call you a cab now.

694
00:48:46,090 --> 00:48:48,968
I can call a cab myself.
I don't need your help.

695
00:48:49,051 --> 00:48:51,303
-No, you take care of her. I'll call one.
-[Youjin] What?

696
00:48:51,387 --> 00:48:53,097
I said I don't need your help. Go.

697
00:48:54,348 --> 00:48:55,808
Just get lost already.

698
00:48:59,979 --> 00:49:01,147
-[soft whirring]
-[latch clicks]

699
00:49:01,230 --> 00:49:02,731
-[chimes]
-[door unlocks]

700
00:49:15,953 --> 00:49:16,996
Damn it.

701
00:49:31,552 --> 00:49:32,553
What the...

702
00:49:59,246 --> 00:50:01,499
Hello? Mom.

703
00:50:01,582 --> 00:50:02,583
Hey.

704
00:50:05,169 --> 00:50:07,213
Oh, no. Did you give her medicine?

705
00:50:09,006 --> 00:50:12,343
Yeah, no wonder Subin got sick.

706
00:50:14,803 --> 00:50:18,224
Okay. All right. Bye.

707
00:50:23,896 --> 00:50:25,022
[Yongseok] What did she say?

708
00:50:25,648 --> 00:50:28,234
Ah, Subin's sick,
so Youjin will stay with her tonight.

709
00:50:28,317 --> 00:50:30,819
She's not sick.
She's just sick from drinking too much.

710
00:50:30,903 --> 00:50:33,656
[exclaims] Do you know
what an appreciation dinner is?

711
00:50:34,865 --> 00:50:37,618
Isn't it just everyone
getting wasted together?

712
00:50:37,701 --> 00:50:40,996
Seohan National University
is where the country's brightest minds go.

713
00:50:41,080 --> 00:50:43,999
It's where they come together
to thank their professors.

714
00:50:44,083 --> 00:50:45,459
Why would she get wasted there?

715
00:50:46,043 --> 00:50:50,089
Mom, anyone can get sick
if they drink too much.

716
00:50:50,172 --> 00:50:52,675
I know. I mean,
Seohan National University students,

717
00:50:52,758 --> 00:50:55,761
the brightest minds in the country,
wouldn't drink that much.

718
00:50:58,722 --> 00:51:03,602
Honey, I saw on TV that kids
get their intelligence from their mothers.

719
00:51:04,812 --> 00:51:08,857
So it turns out
Youjin gets all her brains from me.

720
00:51:09,441 --> 00:51:12,027
What about me? What does that make me?

721
00:51:12,111 --> 00:51:13,821
I take after you too.
What about my grades?

722
00:51:13,904 --> 00:51:15,406
I didn't give birth to you.

723
00:51:15,990 --> 00:51:17,157
Then who did?

724
00:51:17,658 --> 00:51:20,119
My first love in high school.

725
00:51:20,828 --> 00:51:22,288
She gave birth to you.

726
00:51:23,664 --> 00:51:24,915
What? Is that true?

727
00:51:26,333 --> 00:51:29,837
So your first love
is my biological mother or something?

728
00:51:31,046 --> 00:51:33,382
It means your mom is my first love.

729
00:51:33,465 --> 00:51:34,466
Jeez.

730
00:51:35,676 --> 00:51:38,137
Why would you say it like that?
This is so annoying.

731
00:51:38,220 --> 00:51:40,389
-[Miyoung] Hey, go to bed.
-Come on, just a minute.

732
00:51:40,472 --> 00:51:41,557
Go on and get to bed.

733
00:51:44,226 --> 00:51:45,477
I'm so tired.

734
00:52:08,042 --> 00:52:10,002
FAVORITES
23 IMAGES

735
00:52:10,085 --> 00:52:11,086
SELECT ITEMS

736
00:52:13,464 --> 00:52:15,758
23 ITEMS SELECTED
MOVE 23 PHOTOS TO TRASH?

737
00:52:15,841 --> 00:52:17,009
NO FAVORITE PHOTOS

738
00:52:51,794 --> 00:52:54,963
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

739
00:53:02,888 --> 00:53:03,889
Goodness.

740
00:53:16,902 --> 00:53:17,903
[Youngsoo] Professor.

741
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:20,864
How did you...

742
00:53:23,492 --> 00:53:25,452
Professor. Professor!

743
00:53:25,536 --> 00:53:29,998
Professor, wait. Professor!

744
00:53:34,837 --> 00:53:35,921
Get home safe.

745
00:54:28,056 --> 00:54:30,309
<i>The person you are calling is unavailable.</i>

746
00:54:37,191 --> 00:54:38,942
SUBIN, I'M AT YOUR DOOR

747
00:54:39,026 --> 00:54:41,570
INCOMING CALL
PROFESSOR KANG MIRAN

748
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:48,076
QUIET YET POWERFUL
WARM CHARISMA

749
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:50,329
PROFESSOR KANG MIRAN
"A THOUSAND WISHES" PROJECT

750
00:55:04,301 --> 00:55:08,222
I hear he's in the hospital now.
You should go and apologize to him.

751
00:55:08,931 --> 00:55:09,932
Apologize?

752
00:55:11,433 --> 00:55:12,518
Why should I do that?

753
00:55:13,769 --> 00:55:17,481
Violence is never acceptable,
no matter the circumstances.

754
00:55:18,565 --> 00:55:22,069
And to your senior at that?
Don't you have any respect?

755
00:55:26,698 --> 00:55:31,703
If he's my senior,
I think he should act like it first.

756
00:55:31,787 --> 00:55:35,249
I know. He got drunk and made a mistake.

757
00:55:36,208 --> 00:55:39,878
I'm not saying what he did was okay.
But you're from the same school.

758
00:55:39,962 --> 00:55:41,964
Can't you just let
this one little mistake slide?

759
00:55:42,548 --> 00:55:45,008
It's not just a mistake. It's a crime.

760
00:55:45,759 --> 00:55:47,010
So, now it's a crime?

761
00:55:47,761 --> 00:55:50,180
Things can happen
when a man and a woman are dating.

762
00:55:50,847 --> 00:55:51,890
Dating?

763
00:55:52,724 --> 00:55:55,435
They're not. Did Kim Youngsoo
say they were dating?

764
00:55:56,186 --> 00:55:57,688
That's all a lie.

765
00:55:57,771 --> 00:56:00,399
No, that's what Subin said.

766
00:56:01,441 --> 00:56:04,027
She said you and Youngsoo
never really got along.

767
00:56:04,653 --> 00:56:07,531
She said she couldn't be honest
about it because of you.

768
00:56:12,536 --> 00:56:13,745
That can't be true...

769
00:56:16,039 --> 00:56:17,499
That can't be true.

770
00:56:17,583 --> 00:56:20,252
Subin is a kind, soft-hearted girl.

771
00:56:20,335 --> 00:56:22,879
She must've been putting up
with a lot because of you.

772
00:56:27,551 --> 00:56:32,472
Anyway, let's just have you apologize
and leave it at that, okay?

773
00:56:32,556 --> 00:56:34,725
Blowing this up
just embarrasses the school

774
00:56:34,808 --> 00:56:36,560
and reflects badly on us all.

775
00:56:45,944 --> 00:56:48,030
Let's leave it at that and move on.

776
00:56:49,448 --> 00:56:52,993
No. I can't do that.

777
00:56:55,621 --> 00:56:58,332
Whether they were dating or not,
what he did was wrong.

778
00:56:58,415 --> 00:57:00,042
He never should've done it.

779
00:57:00,751 --> 00:57:03,712
He deserved to get hit,
and I have no intention of apologizing.

780
00:57:03,795 --> 00:57:05,964
So you're not going
to listen to me, either?

781
00:57:07,257 --> 00:57:09,051
He didn't act like my senior.

782
00:57:09,885 --> 00:57:11,011
And right now,

783
00:57:12,763 --> 00:57:14,765
I don't think you're acting
like a professor.

784
00:57:15,724 --> 00:57:16,933
What?

785
00:57:17,017 --> 00:57:20,771
Isn't it a teacher's job to correct
and guide students when they do wrong?

786
00:57:21,772 --> 00:57:24,900
Shouldn't that come before the school's
reputation or your pride?

787
00:57:26,610 --> 00:57:29,196
Are you lecturing me right now?

788
00:57:32,157 --> 00:57:34,076
You're obviously so smart.

789
00:57:34,159 --> 00:57:39,122
Who am I to try to guide
or teach someone like you, huh?

790
00:57:39,873 --> 00:57:43,043
You won't listen to a word I say,
so I can hardly call you my student.

791
00:57:47,047 --> 00:57:48,799
If you have nothing further to say,

792
00:57:50,425 --> 00:57:51,927
may I be excused?

793
00:57:55,931 --> 00:57:56,932
Go.

794
00:58:04,356 --> 00:58:08,485
The moment you walk out that door,
you are no longer my student.

795
00:58:09,277 --> 00:58:14,658
So from now on, don't you ever mention
my name or this school to anyone.

796
00:58:16,284 --> 00:58:18,161
Are you threatening me now?

797
00:58:19,037 --> 00:58:22,624
As if someone as proud as you
would feel threatened by this.

798
00:58:46,314 --> 00:58:47,315
Yes.

799
00:58:48,316 --> 00:58:50,235
I know how small this field is.

800
00:58:51,570 --> 00:58:53,363
And honestly, it does scare me.

801
00:58:55,741 --> 00:58:58,118
Thanks to you,
I've learned a valuable lesson.

802
00:58:58,201 --> 00:58:59,619
Thank you for everything.

803
00:59:00,787 --> 00:59:02,080
Take care of yourself.

804
00:59:41,369 --> 00:59:42,370
[passerby] Excuse me.

805
00:59:42,871 --> 00:59:45,040
I don't think you're allowed
to eat in here.

806
00:59:46,416 --> 00:59:49,461
Right. I'm not a student here.

807
00:59:51,755 --> 00:59:52,881
I'm a graduate.

808
00:59:54,132 --> 00:59:56,551
No one can hold my grades over my head

809
00:59:57,594 --> 01:00:02,098
or threaten to keep me from graduating,
so I'm just going to do whatever I want.

810
01:00:05,185 --> 01:00:08,563
I'm free now, just drifting through life
like duckweed on the water.

811
01:00:09,397 --> 01:00:10,649
Mmm-hmm.

812
01:00:15,070 --> 01:00:16,071
What do you think?

813
01:00:19,241 --> 01:00:20,367
[passerby] Mmm...

814
01:00:22,869 --> 01:00:24,830
Yeah, it's beautiful.

815
01:00:27,332 --> 01:00:29,668
[Youjin] It's beautiful
and creative, isn't it?

816
01:00:31,962 --> 01:00:34,256
I think I have a pretty good eye,

817
01:00:36,383 --> 01:00:38,969
but I find clothing a difficult medium
to work with.

818
01:00:40,470 --> 01:00:44,057
Even when I know what I want to convey,
I can't quite turn it into a design,

819
01:00:44,683 --> 01:00:46,268
and I end up copying others' work.

820
01:00:50,897 --> 01:00:53,733
But anyway, that's all just an excuse.

821
01:00:55,610 --> 01:00:56,778
At the end of the day,

822
01:00:56,862 --> 01:01:00,532
I didn't have what it takes
to be an artist or a creative director.

823
01:01:01,449 --> 01:01:04,452
So there's no point blaming anyone else.

824
01:01:05,787 --> 01:01:09,374
It wasn't anyone else's fault.
I just didn't have enough talent.

825
01:01:17,132 --> 01:01:18,133
Hello?

826
01:01:20,427 --> 01:01:21,428
Who is this?

827
01:01:25,765 --> 01:01:26,766
[in English] Yeah.

828
01:01:27,934 --> 01:01:30,729
Ah, I couldn't find
the Natural Sciences building.

829
01:01:31,396 --> 01:01:33,481
So, I'm at the art museum right now.

830
01:01:38,194 --> 01:01:39,905
-[in Korean] Please wait here for a sec.
-Okay.

831
01:01:42,407 --> 01:01:43,783
I checked with the legal team,

832
01:01:43,867 --> 01:01:46,244
and they said it'd be fine
if I have your signature.

833
01:01:49,998 --> 01:01:53,418
But how did you know my phone number?

834
01:01:54,377 --> 01:01:57,964
If you know someone's name and school,
you can easily find their number.

835
01:02:03,011 --> 01:02:06,890
I still haven't
fully forgiven you, though.

836
01:02:08,516 --> 01:02:10,226
But I didn't do anything wrong.

837
01:02:18,443 --> 01:02:19,444
Please follow me.

838
01:02:39,297 --> 01:02:41,341
[Seohyun] I pulled the audio
from the robot,

839
01:02:41,424 --> 01:02:42,425
but it was pretty far away.

840
01:02:43,093 --> 01:02:44,427
Listen to this.

841
01:02:50,684 --> 01:02:51,685
How is it?

842
01:02:53,353 --> 01:02:54,938
Could you turn up the volume?

843
01:02:55,021 --> 01:02:56,022
[Seohyun] Hold on.

844
01:02:57,983 --> 01:02:59,317
That's as loud as it goes.

845
01:03:00,527 --> 01:03:01,778
-It is?
-[Seohyun] Yeah.

846
01:03:08,576 --> 01:03:10,370
-[Minjae] Take a listen.
-Hmm.

847
01:03:18,837 --> 01:03:19,838
Can you hear it?

848
01:03:21,548 --> 01:03:22,757
Do you hear anything?

849
01:03:23,550 --> 01:03:24,551
Uh...

850
01:03:26,845 --> 01:03:27,846
Here.

851
01:03:31,266 --> 01:03:34,394
I made you come all this way for nothing.

852
01:03:34,477 --> 01:03:35,478
I'm sorry.

853
01:03:36,730 --> 01:03:37,731
Not at all.

854
01:03:39,190 --> 01:03:41,359
You went out of your way
to help with all this.

855
01:03:42,277 --> 01:03:44,237
-I'm the one who should be sorry.
-Uh...

856
01:03:47,198 --> 01:03:50,535
And even if there had been evidence,
it wouldn't have helped much.

857
01:03:51,369 --> 01:03:52,370
What?

858
01:03:53,747 --> 01:03:56,958
Apparently, Subin was dating that bastard.

859
01:03:58,168 --> 01:04:01,046
She didn't tell me because she was worried
about how I'd react.

860
01:04:02,047 --> 01:04:03,048
Ah...

861
01:04:03,548 --> 01:04:04,549
I see.

862
01:04:05,884 --> 01:04:09,929
But even if they're dating,
what he did was still wrong.

863
01:04:11,765 --> 01:04:12,766
Right?

864
01:04:13,266 --> 01:04:14,350
Yeah, it's wrong.

865
01:04:15,060 --> 01:04:18,646
And why didn't she tell me
she was dating him?

866
01:04:19,856 --> 01:04:21,983
Isn't it strange that she kept it from me?

867
01:04:23,485 --> 01:04:24,486
Hmm...

868
01:04:25,403 --> 01:04:28,281
No, that's not strange. She can do that.

869
01:04:29,532 --> 01:04:30,533
What?

870
01:04:31,993 --> 01:04:36,289
Even though you two were very close,
she might not have wanted to tell you.

871
01:04:37,457 --> 01:04:38,833
Everyone has secrets.

872
01:04:40,835 --> 01:04:42,045
I don't have any.

873
01:04:42,629 --> 01:04:43,963
I'm sure you do.

874
01:04:44,047 --> 01:04:45,048
I don't.

875
01:04:45,131 --> 01:04:48,718
Haven't you ever
had a crush on someone? Or...

876
01:04:50,720 --> 01:04:53,598
Any habits or weaknesses
you don't want anyone to know about,

877
01:04:54,099 --> 01:04:55,475
or something that hurt you?

878
01:04:56,851 --> 01:04:59,729
Everyone has at least one thing
they can't tell their friends

879
01:04:59,813 --> 01:05:01,189
or even their family.

880
01:05:03,817 --> 01:05:06,778
Do you have something like that?

881
01:05:07,362 --> 01:05:09,030
No, I don't.

882
01:05:14,119 --> 01:05:16,871
Well, you're graduating soon anyway.

883
01:05:18,164 --> 01:05:21,167
Try to put the bad experience
behind you and make a fresh start.

884
01:05:23,002 --> 01:05:24,003
A fresh start...

885
01:05:25,130 --> 01:05:28,508
Your friend has her own life to live,
and so do you.

886
01:05:29,342 --> 01:05:32,137
You're studying
mechanical engineering, right?

887
01:05:32,220 --> 01:05:35,431
Yes, I'm doing my PhD in robotics.

888
01:05:36,224 --> 01:05:39,727
I haven't actually earned the degree yet.
I'm still just a student.

889
01:05:42,605 --> 01:05:46,109
What first drew you
to mechanical engineering?

890
01:05:46,985 --> 01:05:48,987
There's usually a story behind it.

891
01:05:49,821 --> 01:05:50,947
There is.

892
01:05:52,740 --> 01:05:54,325
Have you ever read <i>Slam Dunk?</i>

893
01:05:55,410 --> 01:05:56,870
<i>-Slam Dunk?</i>
-[Minjae] Yes.

894
01:05:56,953 --> 01:05:57,954
The comic series?

895
01:05:59,414 --> 01:06:00,582
No, I haven't read it.

896
01:06:02,041 --> 01:06:04,669
You haven't? You really should.
It's a masterpiece.

897
01:06:06,546 --> 01:06:07,547
Uh...

898
01:06:08,423 --> 01:06:11,843
How I got into mechanical engineering
is kind of like <i>Slam Dunk.</i>

899
01:06:13,052 --> 01:06:15,305
[announcer] <i>The 687 bus</i>
<i>will arrive shortly.</i>

900
01:06:15,388 --> 01:06:16,389
The bus is here.

901
01:06:21,144 --> 01:06:22,353
Aren't you going to get on?

902
01:06:22,437 --> 01:06:24,272
Ah, this one doesn't go to my place.

903
01:06:28,318 --> 01:06:30,069
-[card reader beeps]
-[door hisses]

904
01:06:40,663 --> 01:06:44,042
We've met at a bus stop before.

905
01:06:44,876 --> 01:06:46,127
Do you remember?

906
01:06:48,588 --> 01:06:50,048
Do you remember?

907
01:06:50,882 --> 01:06:51,883
Ah...

908
01:06:55,803 --> 01:06:59,182
So, about <i>Slam Dunk.</i> How is it similar?

909
01:06:59,265 --> 01:07:00,266
Ah.

910
01:07:00,934 --> 01:07:04,145
Before Hanamichi Sakuragi
first joins the basketball team,

911
01:07:04,229 --> 01:07:08,441
Haruko Akagi asks him,
"Do you like basketball?"

912
01:07:09,025 --> 01:07:14,697
And he goes,
"Yes, I like it. Very, very much..."

913
01:07:14,781 --> 01:07:15,782
What?

914
01:07:19,410 --> 01:07:22,747
[yelling] "Yes, I like it.
Very, very much."

915
01:08:08,209 --> 01:08:12,171
BETWEEN STEPS

916
01:08:12,255 --> 01:08:15,550
But why do you suddenly want to switch
to a completely different major?

917
01:08:15,633 --> 01:08:19,178
He was sitting side by side with a woman,
looking at something on a laptop.

918
01:08:19,262 --> 01:08:22,473
[Youjin] <i>Boyfriend? Why do you care</i>
<i>if I have a boyfriend or not?</i>

919
01:08:22,974 --> 01:08:24,767
[Minjae] <i>What do you mean, be honest?</i>

920
01:08:25,351 --> 01:08:27,270
[Hangyeol] <i>Are you dating that woman?</i>

921
01:08:27,812 --> 01:08:29,605
[Youjin] <i>Park Minjae</i>
<i>isn't exactly my type, either.</i>

922
01:08:29,731 --> 01:08:31,316
<i>I can't stand guys like him.</i>

923
01:08:31,899 --> 01:08:34,193
[Minjae] <i>What were you doing</i>
<i>while she caused trouble?</i>

924
01:08:35,361 --> 01:08:37,780
[Youjin] <i>He's smart, handsome, and tall.</i>

925
01:08:37,864 --> 01:08:39,240
<i>What if he doesn't like me?</i>
